      "name": "robbritt",
      "username": "robbritt",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/b487fb/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2014-09-02T14:48:27.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I picked up SotM EE at Dragoncon over the weekend from the Foambrain Games booth. My son and I played it that night, and we bought the RC/IR expansion the next day as we were very impressed. I had seen the game before at various LGS, but the ladies at the Foambrain booth are avid players and really sold the game well. I've already pre-ordered the Cosmos expansion, and will pick up Vengeance, Timelines, and whatever mini-expansions I can find in the future (bought Silver Gulch at the con as well). I was a bit surprised to find out that SotM has a \"lifespan\" so to speak. I know we've got time as I believe we are a couple of expansions away from the end of the story. This does lead to my question. Once the current storyline ends, will GTG stop making SotM in its current form? Or will they start another arc? Some of this info may not have been released yet, so the whole plan may not be known. Could someone summarize what is known about GTG's plans about after \"The End\"?</p>",
